      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_5",
        on: "start",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Hamel",
            text: _("Aiglondur, what ye ha’ found is disturbing, for all it seems a small thing. I make known to ye Angarthing, loremaster in training, who recognized the mark on it."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("The mark on this cloak-pin is that of our kin at Kal Kartha in the eastern hills, from whom we’ve heard nothing since before Tallin broke the orcish occupation of Knalga. It troubles us that an orc should have come to possess it; no outsider should know even that loremasters exist, let alone come near enough one to get this."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Hamel",
            text: _("I fear some grave ill may have become Kal Kartha."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("And I fear for the Hammer of Thursagan. Our kin at Kal Kartha have been its keepers since a hero of their line recovered it from the Caverns of Flame, centuries ago."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Aiglondur",
            text: _("The Hammer of Thursagan?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("Aye. The very tool with which our greatest runesmith made the Sceptre of Fire. But it is ancient, far older than Thursagan; he was but the last to wield it, and our oldest histories hint that this very hammer was used to forge the dwarves themselves in the heart of the earth."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Aiglondur",
            text: _("But if the dwarves of Kal Kartha have held it all this time, why has none wielded it since Thursagan?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Hamel",
            text: _("Because when Thursagan burned to death with his hand on the Hammer, all the runemasters and arcanisters then living — all those who had sworn to the craft and bound themselves to the power o’ the Hammer — dropped dead without a mark on them, all struck down at the same moment. Their craft secrets died with them. That is why there are nae runesmiths among the Dwarves today, and sorely we miss them."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("That is what is said, my lord Hamel, and it is true. Except this; the Order of Loremasters has given me leave to reveal that the craft secrets were not, actually, quite as lost as we believed."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Hamel",
            text: _("What is this ye say? Nae lost?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("Aye. Ye’ll recall that in repairing the western galleries we cleared a small cave-in hard by where Thursagan himself once had a workshop here, before he left to study in solitude in the further North."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Hamel",
            text: _("And ye found something?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("A book. Thursagan’s book, in a secret and locked compartment he must have dug from the living rock himself by unaided runecraft. The cave-in breached it. It has taken us great effort to puzzle out his code. But it might be that, with the book and the Hammer to hand, we could train and initiate runesmiths once more."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Hamel",
            text: _("And for what cause ha’ I heard naught o’ this?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("My lord, the find was very recent. We are still deciphering the book. And there is this: with the Hammer at Kal Kartha and the book here, the question of which holding shall have the training of the new runesmiths in its hands would be... delicate."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("We feared stirring up a controversy before the book was even properly understood."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Hamel",
            text: _("I’ll grant that was well thought, even if I am nae entirely pleased to have been kept in the dark. But ye came to me with a request, and I think I ken what it will be."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Aiglondur",
            text: _("That is obvious; the Order of Loremasters wants to send an expedition to Kal Kartha to find what has become of our kindred and the Hammer."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("Indeed, Lord Hamel, that is what we came to ask."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Hamel",
            text: _("And you spoke my guess, Aiglondur. Are you nae kin of mine?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Aiglondur",
            text: _("Your great-nephew, my lord."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Hamel",
            text: _("Ye’re young and not tested... but ye have the rank, and ye’ve shown the wits to use it well. I have decided. You and Angarthing will fare to Kal Kartha together, as soon as may be, with the best men of your guard."),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scenario_move",
            unit: "Angarthing",
            x: 10,
            y: 6,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:modify_unit",
            side: 1,
            filter: "%7B%22tag%22%3A%22filter%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A%22Angarthing%22%7D%2C%22children%22%3A%5B%5D%7D",
            id: "Angarthing",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Aiglondur",
            text: _("Aye, my Lord Hamel."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Angarthing",
            text: _("The Order thanks you, Lord Hamel."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Aiglondur",
            text: _("We must make haste; winter approaches, and travel over the mountains will soon grow dangerous."),
          },
          {
            tag: "win",
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
]
